---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="SIP Calculator – Calculate Monthly Investment Returns & Step-Up SIP"
  description="Estimate the potential future value of your monthly investments, compare regular and step-up contributions, and view your projected growth over time."
  category="Finance"
  calculatorName="SIP Calculator"
  slug="sip-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'sip calculator',
    'sip calculator india',
    'step up sip calculator',
    'sip calculator sbi',
    'sbi sip calculator',
    'sip calculator with step up',
    'sip calculator groww',
    'hdfc sip calculator',
    'mutual fund sip calculator',
    'sip calculator hdfc'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- SIP CALCULATOR MODE SELECTOR TABS -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-2.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 overflow-x-auto pb-1 text-xs font-semibold scrollbar-thin">
        <button type="button" class="btn-sip-tab active shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-4 py-1.5 font-bold text-white shadow-xs cursor-pointer" data-mode="regular">Regular SIP 📈</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-sip-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-1.5 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-mode="stepup">Step Up SIP (Top-Up) 🚀</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- QUICK PRESETS BAR -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-xs">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mr-1 flex items-center gap-1">
          <span>⚡</span> Presets:
        </span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-mode="regular" data-amt="5000" data-rate="12" data-years="10">📈 Regular (₹5k/mo @ 12%, 10 Yrs)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-mode="stepup" data-amt="5000" data-rate="12" data-years="10" data-step-type="percentage" data-step-val="10">🚀 Step-Up 10% (₹5k/mo @ 12%, 10 Yrs)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-mode="stepup" data-amt="5000" data-rate="12" data-years="10" data-step-type="fixed" data-step-val="500">💰 Fixed Step-Up (+₹500/Yr)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-mode="regular" data-amt="10000" data-rate="12" data-years="20">🏆 Long-Term Wealth (₹10k/mo @ 12%, 20 Yrs)</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN CALCULATOR FORM CONTAINER -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/30 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20 sm:p-7">
      
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
        <h2 id="sip-panel-title" class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>📈</span> Mutual Fund SIP Calculator
        </h2>
        <p id="sip-panel-desc" class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Estimate the potential future value of your monthly investments, compare regular and step-up contributions, and view your projected growth over time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <form id="form-sip" class="mt-4 space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
        
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <!-- Monthly Investment -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-monthly-sip" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Monthly Investment (₹)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inp-monthly-sip" value="5000" step="500" min="100" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="5,000" />
          </div>

          <!-- Expected Annual Return Rate -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-return-rate" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Expected Return Rate (% p.a.)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inp-return-rate" value="12" step="0.5" min="0" max="50" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="12" />
          </div>

          <!-- Investment Time Horizon -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-investment-years" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Investment Duration (Years)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inp-investment-years" value="10" step="1" min="1" max="40" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="10" />
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Optional Step Up SIP Configuration Row (Hidden in Regular Mode) -->
        <div id="row-stepup-config" class="hidden rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>🚀</span> Annual Step-Up (Top-Up) Settings
          </span>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="sel-stepup-type" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Step-Up Type</label>
              <select id="sel-stepup-type" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
                <option value="percentage" selected>Percentage Increase (% per year)</option>
                <option value="fixed">Fixed Amount Increase (₹ per year)</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="inp-stepup-val" id="lbl-stepup-val" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Annual Increase (%)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-stepup-val" value="10" step="1" min="1" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="10" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2">
          <button type="submit" id="btn-calc-sip" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">
            Calculate SIP →
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-clear-sip" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer">
            Clear (✕)
          </button>
        </div>

        <p id="err-sip" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-2.5 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

      </form>

      <!-- RESULTS PRESENTATION SECTION (Hidden Initially) -->
      <div id="sip-results-section" class="hidden mt-6 space-y-5">
        
        <!-- Main Highlight Card -->
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-emerald-200 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-emerald-50/40 to-emerald-100/50 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/5 dark:border-emerald-900/60 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-emerald-950/30 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-emerald-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">Estimated Future Value (Maturity Corpus)</span>
              <div id="res-future-val" class="mt-1 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 11,61,695</div>
            </div>
            <div class="sm:text-right">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Wealth Gain Multiplier:</span>
              <div id="res-wealth-multiplier" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1.94x</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Total Invested Amount</div>
              <div id="res-total-invested" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 6,00,000</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Estimated Returns</div>
              <div id="res-est-returns" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 5,61,695</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Investment Duration</div>
              <div id="res-duration-text" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">10 Years</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Final Monthly SIP</div>
              <div id="res-final-sip" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">₹ 5,000 / mo</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- VISUAL BREAKDOWN WITH SVG DONUT -->
        <div id="res-visual-breakdown" class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mb-4 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>📊</span> Invested Amount vs Estimated Wealth Growth
          </h3>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-around gap-6">
            
            <!-- SVG Donut -->
            <div class="relative w-40 h-40 flex items-center justify-center">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 36 36" class="w-full h-full transform -rotate-90">
                <!-- Background circle (Invested) -->
                <circle cx="18" cy="18" r="15.91549430918954" fill="transparent" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="3.8"></circle>
                <!-- Foreground circle (Returns) -->
                <circle id="svg-donut-returns" cx="18" cy="18" r="15.91549430918954" fill="transparent" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="3.8" stroke-dasharray="48.4 51.6" stroke-dashoffset="0"></circle>
              </svg>
              <div class="absolute text-center">
                <span class="text-[11px] font-bold text-slate-400 block">SPLIT</span>
                <span class="text-xs font-black text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">100%</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Legend & Stats -->
            <div class="space-y-3 text-xs w-full sm:w-auto">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-6 p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-blue-50/50 dark:bg-blue-950/20 border border-blue-100 dark:border-blue-900/40">
                <span class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">
                  <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-blue-600 inline-block"></span> Invested Amount:
                </span>
                <span id="txt-legend-invested" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">₹ 6,00,000 (51.6%)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-6 p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50/50 dark:bg-emerald-950/20 border border-emerald-100 dark:border-emerald-900/40">
                <span class="flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">
                  <span class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 inline-block"></span> Estimated Returns:
                </span>
                <span id="txt-legend-returns" class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">₹ 5,61,695 (48.4%)</span>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SIP INVESTMENT SCHEDULE & SELECTIVE PDF DOWNLOAD -->
        <div id="res-schedule-card" class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>📅</span> SIP Investment Schedule
            </h3>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold">
              <button type="button" id="btn-sip-yearly" class="rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-2.5 py-1 text-white shadow-2xs cursor-pointer">Yearly Summary</button>
              <button type="button" id="btn-sip-monthly" class="rounded-lg border border-slate-300 px-2.5 py-1 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer">Monthly Schedule</button>
              <button type="button" id="btn-sip-download-pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer" title="Download active schedule as PDF">
                <span>📄</span> <span id="txt-btn-sip-pdf">Download PDF</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto max-h-96 scrollbar-thin">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold sticky top-0">
                <tr>
                  <th id="th-sip-period" class="p-2.5 rounded-l-lg">Year</th>
                  <th id="th-sip-deposit" class="p-2.5 text-right">Annual Investment</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Total Invested</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">Estimated Returns</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right rounded-r-lg font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Portfolio Value</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="sip-schedule-tbody" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
                <!-- Injected by JS -->
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATIONAL SEO ARTICLE SLOT (Styled matching age.astro) -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="sip-content">
      <h2>How to Use This SIP Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Planning your monthly investments takes just a few steps with this calculator:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Enter your monthly investment amount:</strong> Input the sum in Indian Rupees (₹) you plan to invest every month.</li>
        <li><strong>Enter the expected annual rate of return:</strong> Specify an estimated annual growth rate (e.g., 12% p.a. for long-term equity mutual funds).</li>
        <li><strong>Choose your investment duration:</strong> Select the investment horizon in years (e.g., 5, 10, 15, or 20 years).</li>
        <li><strong>Select Regular SIP or Step-Up SIP:</strong> Choose between a fixed monthly contribution or an increasing annual contribution.</li>
        <li><strong>Configure Step-Up SIP (optional):</strong> If using Step-Up SIP, enter how much your contribution should increase each year (as a percentage like 10% or a fixed rupee amount like ₹500).</li>
        <li><strong>Click Calculate:</strong> View your estimated future value, cumulative amount invested, and projected compounding returns.</li>
        <li><strong>Explore Schedules & PDF Export:</strong> Switch between the <em>Yearly Summary</em> and <em>Monthly Schedule</em>, or click <em>Download PDF</em> to save the active schedule.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>SIP Calculation Example</h2>
      <p>
        To understand how regular monthly contributions compound over time, consider a practical long-term investment scenario:
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-2">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          <div><span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs">Monthly Contribution:</span> ₹5,000</div>
          <div><span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs">Assumed Annual Return:</span> 12% p.a.</div>
          <div><span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs">Investment Horizon:</span> 15 Years (180 Months)</div>
        </div>
        <hr class="border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 my-2" />
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 font-bold">
          <div>
            <span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs font-normal">Total Invested Capital:</span>
            <span class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 text-base">₹9,00,000</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs font-normal">Estimated Compounding Returns:</span>
            <span class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 text-base">₹16,22,880</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs font-normal">Estimated Future Value:</span>
            <span class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300 text-base">₹25,22,880</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        In this example, your total out-of-pocket investment of <strong>₹9,00,000</strong> compounds to an <strong>estimated future value of ₹25,22,880</strong>, generating <strong>₹16,22,880</strong> in estimated returns. This demonstrates the potential of compounding over a 15-year horizon, where wealth generation exceeds the total invested principal.
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
        * Note: These figures are mathematical estimates for planning purposes. Actual mutual fund returns depend on market performance, NAV movements, and fund management fees.
      </p>

      <h2>What Is a Systematic Investment Plan (SIP)?</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>Systematic Investment Plan (SIP)</strong> is an investment method where an individual contributes a predetermined fixed or stepping amount at regular intervals (typically monthly) into a mutual fund scheme. Rather than trying to time market highs and lows with a single large deposit, SIP encourages disciplined, periodic investing.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Do Investors Use SIPs?</h2>
      <p>
        Systematic investing offers practical advantages for personal wealth management:
      </p>
      
      <h3>Investing Regularly</h3>
      <p>
        Automating monthly contributions establishes a steady savings routine, making wealth creation an ongoing financial habit rather than an irregular afterthought.
      </p>

      <h3>Starting with Smaller Amounts</h3>
      <p>
        Most mutual funds allow investors to start SIPs with as little as ₹500 per month, removing the barrier of needing large lump-sum capital upfront.
      </p>

      <h3>Rupee-Cost Averaging</h3>
      <p>
        When financial markets dip, your fixed monthly installment purchases more mutual fund units at lower Net Asset Values (NAVs). When markets rise, you purchase fewer units at higher NAVs. Over time, this averages out your acquisition cost per unit without requiring market timing.
      </p>

      <h3>Long-Term Compounding Potential</h3>
      <p>
        Earnings generated by your investments are reinvested, producing their own subsequent returns. Over multi-year horizons (10, 15, or 20+ years), compounding can significantly amplify portfolio growth.
      </p>

      <h3>Flexibility</h3>
      <p>
        Depending on the fund house and platform guidelines, investors can modify, increase, pause, or redeem their SIP investments as their financial circumstances evolve.
      </p>

      <h2>Regular SIP vs Step-Up SIP</h2>
      <p>
        Understanding how contribution adjustments impact long-term portfolio growth helps align investments with career progression:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Regular SIP:</strong> The monthly contribution stays identical across the entire tenure (e.g., investing ₹5,000 every month for 10 years). It offers predictable budgeting and straightforward tracking.</li>
        <li><strong>Step-Up SIP:</strong> The monthly contribution increases periodically (e.g., starting at ₹5,000 per month in Year 1, then stepping up by 10% to ₹5,500 in Year 2, ₹6,050 in Year 3, and so on). This mirrors annual salary increments and substantially accelerates corpus building.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <em>Important Consideration:</em> A step-up strategy requires disciplined cash-flow planning to ensure future stepped-up contributions remain comfortable within your family budget.
      </p>

      <h2>SIP vs Lump Sum Investment</h2>
      <p>
        Choosing between a periodic SIP and a one-time lump-sum deposit depends on your capital availability, risk appetite, and market outlook:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Factor</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">SIP (Systematic Investment)</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Lump Sum (One-Time)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Investment Pattern</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Periodic installments (Monthly / Quarterly)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Single upfront deposit</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Upfront Capital Required</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Low (starts from ₹500/month)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">High (requires ready pool of savings)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Timing Risk</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Low (mitigated via rupee-cost averaging)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">High (entering at a market peak can hurt short-term returns)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Investment Discipline</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">High (automates monthly savings habit)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Variable (depends on opportunistic deployments)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Market Entry</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Gradual across bull and bear cycles</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Immediate all-at-once exposure</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Flexibility</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Can pause, increase, or adjust amounts</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Fixed at inception; new deposits require fresh orders</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Suitable Situations</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Salaried earners with recurring monthly income</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Windfall gains, bonuses, or proceeds from asset sales</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>How Much Should You Invest in a SIP?</h2>
      <p>
        Determining your ideal monthly SIP amount depends on your individual financial objectives and disposable cash flow. A practical planning roadmap includes:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Define clear financial goals:</strong> Categorize targets by horizon (e.g., child education in 10 years, retirement in 20 years).</li>
        <li><strong>Estimate the target corpus:</strong> Calculate how much capital may be required, keeping inflation in mind.</li>
        <li><strong>Select realistic return assumptions:</strong> Use reasonable annualized expectations (e.g., 10%–12% for diversified equity) rather than speculative outliers.</li>
        <li><strong>Test scenarios with the calculator:</strong> Adjust your monthly deposit, tenure, and step-up rate to find an achievable monthly savings figure.</li>
        <li><strong>Maintain emergency reserves:</strong> Ensure your SIP contribution is budgeted comfortably without compromising your emergency fund or short-term liquidity needs.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>How SIP Returns Are Estimated</h2>
      <p>
        Our SIP calculator evaluates compounding growth on monthly cash flows using the future value annuity formula:
      </p>
      <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100/80 p-4 font-mono text-sm dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
        <div>FV = P × [((1 + r)ⁿ − 1) ÷ r] × (1 + r)</div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Here, <strong>P</strong> represents the monthly installment, <strong>r</strong> is the monthly rate of return (annual return ÷ 12 ÷ 100), and <strong>n</strong> is the number of months. In Step-Up mode, each 12-month tranche is adjusted for the stepped-up contribution and compounded through maturity.
      </p>

      <h2>Common Mistakes When Using a SIP Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Avoid these frequent pitfalls when evaluating investment projections:
      </p>

      <h3>Assuming Returns Are Guaranteed</h3>
      <p>
        A SIP calculator provides mathematical projections based on assumed static rates. Real-world market returns fluctuate year to year and are never fixed or guaranteed.
      </p>

      <h3>Using Unrealistic Return Expectations</h3>
      <p>
        Inputting overly aggressive returns (such as 20% or 25% annualized) inflates future estimates and can derail financial planning. Using balanced estimates (10%–13%) provides a more reliable foundation.
      </p>

      <h3>Ignoring Investment Duration</h3>
      <p>
        Compounding exerts its strongest impact in the latter half of an investment horizon. Stopping a SIP too early significantly reduces total wealth creation.
      </p>

      <h3>Forgetting to Account for Inflation</h3>
      <p>
        While a ₹1 Crore corpus looks substantial today, inflation erodes purchasing power over 15 to 20 years. Consider stepping up contributions to keep pace with cost-of-living increases.
      </p>

      <h3>Confusing Total Investment with Estimated Returns</h3>
      <p>
        Always check the distinction between the principal capital you deposited out of pocket versus the estimated compounding gain generated over time.
      </p>

      <h3>Increasing SIP Contributions Without Planning</h3>
      <p>
        Setting an overly steep annual step-up percentage without considering future cash flow may lead to premature SIP cancellations.
      </p>

      <h2>Using a SIP Calculator Across Different Investment Platforms</h2>
      <p>
        Whether you are comparing SIP options available through a bank or investment platform, such as SBI, HDFC, Groww, or another provider, the investment projection depends primarily on the amount invested, time horizon, and assumed rate of return.
      </p>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
        * Notice: This calculator is an independent educational tool and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by SBI, HDFC, Groww, or any other financial institution or investment platform.
      </p>

      <h2>Important Assumptions and Risk Information</h2>
      <p>
        Please review the following essential principles regarding this calculator:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Projection Tool Only:</strong> This calculator provides simulated projections based on mathematical models and user-provided inputs. It does not provide financial or tax advice.</li>
        <li><strong>Market Risks:</strong> Mutual funds and equity-linked investments are subject to market risks. Portfolio values may fluctuate, and capital loss is possible.</li>
        <li><strong>Fees & Taxes:</strong> Calculations do not subtract fund expense ratios, exit loads, Securities Transaction Tax (STT), or Capital Gains Tax (LTCG/STCG) applicable upon redemption.</li>
        <li><strong>Inflation Impact:</strong> Projections do not adjust nominal future values for inflation unless modeled via step-up contributions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

